    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **28 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation following the codebase's existing pattern for read-only derived owner fields (like `membershipNumber` and `membershipTier`), which are computed getters on the `Owner` entity that MapStruct maps by name into the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `getLocality()` getter returning the canonical region string, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` field to the `OwnerDto` schema so the generated DTO exposes it and MapStruct wires the getter into the JSON response.\n\nThe `Cp17Tests` acceptance test (Sydney\u2192`NSW`, and a random unknown city\u2192`UNKNOWN`) passes, and all 28 existing tests remain green.",
